{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788999645,"nonce":"cMhGjDBtzKSQGdVPT/6wHaDw1vM=","message":"REPRODUCIBLE without lifting any gate, contradicting my earlier note that this needed the i64 refusal relaxed. It fires on an i8 element, which lanes_fit permits (8 bits x VF 4 = 32, inside one machine vector).\n\n    class TestUI8Wrap {\n      static function main() {\n        var a:hl.UI8 = 250; var i = 0;\n        while (i \u003c 10) { a = a + 1; i++; }\n        Sys.println(\"a=\" + (a : Int));\n        var b:hl.UI8 = 200; b = b * 2;\n        Sys.println(\"b=\" + (b : Int));\n        var c:hl.UI16 = 65530; c = c + 10;\n        Sys.println(\"c=\" + (c : Int));\n        var d:hl.UI8 = 5; d = -d;\n        Sys.println(\"d=\" + (d : Int));\n        var e:hl.UI8 = 255; e++;\n        Sys.println(\"e=\" + (e : Int));\n      }\n    }\n\n    haxe -hl ui8.hl -main TestUI8Wrap -cp .\n    ash --build ui8bin ui8.hl\n      Error: 1 function(s) could not be lowered ...\n        findex=24: VecSplat destination is not a vector\n\nASH_AIR_NO_WIDEN=1 clears it and the binary builds and runs, so the widener is\nthe producer. The AIR report shows widen firing exactly once on this program\n(replaced=1) and not at all on variants without the UI8 loop.\n\nfindex 24 is a 3-op constructor with no loop of its own, so the VecSplat reaches\nit by INLINING -- it calls findex 22, and at O3 the inliner runs before the\nwidener. That is worth knowing before looking for the bug inside findex 24.\n\nThe same reproducer also exposes a widener SOUNDNESS bug, filed separately.","files":null}]}